--- a/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
+++ b/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ The following options are provided to configure the output:
 * **`SEPARATOR`**:
     The text string used to set the footnote separator. Defaults to `:`.
 
+* **`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`**:
+    Whether to order footnotes by footnote content rather than by footnote
+    label. Defaults to `False`.
+
+    By default, footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are
+    first referenced in the document. Footnotes referenced from within other
+    footnotes follow the footnote containing them, and footnotes which are never
+    referenced are listed last in definition order. When `True`, footnotes are
+    instead numbered and listed in the order of their definitions.
+
 A trivial example:
 
 ```python
